Guest reset kills the VM when a GL listener is attached, and 0001 does not
cover it. On reset the console hands dbus_gl_gfx_switch() a fresh
DisplaySurface whose GL texture has not been created yet, and it passes
ds->texture (0) straight to dbus_scanout_texture(), which asserts:

    qemu-system-x86_64: ui/dbus-listener.c:518:
        dbus_scanout_texture: Assertion `tex_id' failed.

0001 makes the render-node context current inside the DisplayGLCtx texture
hooks, which fixes the case where the texture is created without a context;
it does nothing for a switch that arrives before any texture exists. Both
were reproduced on a 2D (viogpudo) Windows guest: stock Ubuntu QEMU 10.2.1
and a 0001-patched 10.0.12 crash identically on `virsh reboot`.

There is nothing to show for a surface with no texture, and the next
gfx_update/switch scans out once one exists, so skip it. With this guard the
guest reboots with the listener attached and frames resume on the far side.

--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -797,7 +797,7 @@
 
     ddl->ds = new_surface;
     ddl->ds_share = SHARE_KIND_NONE;
-    if (ddl->ds) {
+    if (ddl->ds && ddl->ds->texture) {
         int width = surface_width(ddl->ds);
         int height = surface_height(ddl->ds);
